# Lab names the lab's own resolver does not serve, answered by the server's
# dnsmasq instead. Same layout as /etc/hosts: an address, then one or more
# names. server-bootstrap.sh turns each line into a host-record in
# /etc/dnsmasq.d/lab-split-dns.conf, so a change takes effect on its next run.
#
# Copy to ~/.config/client-lab.hosts. Never commit the real file.
#
# Every name must sit inside LAB_ZONE: only that zone is pointed at the server,
# so a record for any other name is never asked for. The address must be
# reachable from the clients, which in practice means inside LAB_SUBNET.

10.20.7.47   git.corp.example
